    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28037" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mărī^a</span></b> , ae,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a female proper name</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Mary, the mother of Jesus</i> (eccl. Lat.), <i><span class="en">Vulg. Matt.
				2, 11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marĭa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Psych. 88</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Apoth. 643</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Sedul. Car. Pasch. 2, 49</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marīa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Hymn. 1, 53</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">54</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Mary Magdalene</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Johan. 20, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sedul. 4,
			142</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Mary of Bethany, sister of Lazarus and Martha</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Vulg. Johan. 11, 1</span></i>.</div>
